# STRICT.md

Optional strict appendix. Read for strict profile or high-risk tasks.

## HITL before

- New dependency installation.
- Database schema changes.
- CI/CD changes.
- Auth, permissions, billing, encryption, data retention, or migration beyond plan.
- Network access.
- Writes outside workspace.

## Escalation format

```text
Triggered rule:
Evidence:
Options:
Recommendation:
Minimum human decision needed:
```

## Long-running process pattern

Foreground dev servers block agents.

Use background process + log + PID + cleanup:

```bash
mkdir -p .codex_artifacts/logs
nohup <dev-server-command> > .codex_artifacts/logs/devserver.log 2>&1 &
echo $! > .codex_artifacts/logs/devserver.pid
# run checks
kill "$(cat .codex_artifacts/logs/devserver.pid)" || true
```

## Validation cost policy

- Fast gate: every milestone.
- Targeted gate: after behavior changes.
- Full gate: before review freeze.
- E2E / visual: before review freeze or UI behavior changes.
- Flaky / expensive checks: record once; avoid repair loops without new evidence.
